# PolicyLens configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your key:
#   PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED: Google Gemini API key
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey -- no credit card
# needed.
#
# MEASURE YOUR BUDGET BEFORE PLANNING A BATCH RUN. The free tier is charged
# per MODEL per day, and for gemini-3.8-flash the API reports a limit of
# 20 requests/day (quotaId GenerateRequestsPerDayPerProjectPerModel-FreeTier)
# with a ~22 hour reset. One answer costs 2-5 calls, so that is four or five
# questions a day on a single model.
#
# This is why POLICYLENS_FALLBACK_MODELS below is a chain of sibling models
# rather than one spare: each model name has its own daily bucket on the same
# key, so the chain multiplies what one key can do. Run
#   python scripts/check_models.py
# to see how much of the chain is callable right now.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_gemini_key_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: Groq API key (last link in the fallback chain)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The chain's Gemini entries all fail together in a Google-wide outage, which
# is what this one is for. Free key at https://console.groq.com/keys -- also no
# credit card. Note that a Groq key is granted a SUBSET of the published
# catalogue, so the published model list is not what your key can call -- the
# key this was developed against reaches no llama chat model at all. If it
# fails with "model_not_found", ask the key itself:
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $GROQ_API_KEY" https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/models
# then set POLICYLENS_FALLBACK_MODELS to a chat model from that response.
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key_here_optional

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: overrides for values in src/config.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Swap the model without touching code. Any LiteLLM model string works,
# e.g. groq/openai/gpt-oss-120b or openai/gpt-4o-mini.
#
# The free tier's model names are NOT stable -- Google retires them and
# refuses the old name for newly created keys. If every LLM call fails, run
#   python scripts/check_models.py --list
# to see what your key can actually call, and set it here.
# POLICYLENS_MODEL=gemini/gemini-3.8-flash

# Minimum cosine similarity for a retrieved chunk to count as relevant.
# Raise it to make the agent abstain more readily, lower it to answer more.
# POLICYLENS_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD=0.30

# Models to try, in order, when the one before fails. Each Gemini model has
# its own free-tier daily bucket, so more entries means more questions per day.
# POLICYLENS_FALLBACK_MODELS=gemini/gemini-3.5-flash,gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# Seconds to wait between LLM calls, to stay inside free-tier per-minute
# limits during batch evaluation. Lower it for faster interactive use.
# POLICYLENS_LLM_THROTTLE_SECONDS=4.0

# DEBUG shows retrieval scores and full prompts; INFO is the default.
# POLICYLENS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
